WEBVTT

00:00:58.280 --> 00:00:58.900
and that's the

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:34.740
That was footage from surveillance cameras at the station.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:38.200
The death of one of the FBI agents is captured on here.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.200
Hmm...

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.850
Let's see the following scenes again.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.310
Ray Penber passing the ticket gate on his way in,

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:46.510
then him boarding the train, and finally the part where he dies on the platform.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:47.920
Okay.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.110
Let's see.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:51.000
I think it's next to that.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.740
Oh, here it is.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.320
Um, so based on the records I have here,

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:00.000
Ray Penber comes through the west entrance of Shinjuku Station at 3:11 p.m.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.780
Then at 3:13 he boards a train on the Yamanote line.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:06.150
But even if he was following someone at that time,

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:10.620
I think it's going to be very difficult for us to draw any real conclusions from this blurry video.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.760
Then at exactly 4:42 p.m. a...

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.590
Mm. Oh, thank you very much, Watari.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:22.920
Um, and at 4:42 p.m. he exits the train at Tokyo Station and dies on the platform.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.550
It's quite strange, don't you think?

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.960
I'm sorry, what do you find strange?

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.000
Yeah, what is it? Did you notice something?

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:37.380
Hmm. We know that Ray Penberg got on the train and then an hour and a half later he got off and died on the platform.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:42.410
But the Yamanote line only takes an hour to complete its circuit, and more importantly, there's the envelope.

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:43.860
What do you mean?

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:50.140
He's holding what looks like an envelope when he passes through the ticket gate.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.200
Huh? You're right! It's there under his arm!

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:59.030
But in the footage right before his death, it's gone! I can't believe you actually caught that!

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:03.460
Well, I don't see an envelope on this list of his personal effects.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:06.350
Which means it was left on the train.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:09.920
And if you watch closely at the very end here,

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:14.390
it seems like he's straining to look inside the train before the doors close.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:15.680
You can see right here.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:18.300
If that's the case, do you think it could mean something?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.000
Wouldn't it be interesting if Kira was on that train?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.360
That's impossible!

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.230
I admit, I find it hard to believe as well.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:30.000
There's no reason for Kira to come to the scene of his own crime when he can kill from a distance.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:36.720
Maybe he was counting on us to make that assumption and figured he could get away with such a bold move.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.290
What's going on with you, Light?

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:52.250
You haven't stopped writing criminals' names in the Death Note for four days straight, so what are you trying to prove?

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.760
I don't see the point in writing these names weeks in advance. I've never seen the Death Note used like this.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.100
Consider it insurance.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:00.000
Suppose the...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.200
son of the detective superintendent of the NPA was hospitalized. If criminals

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.240
stopped dying at the same time it wouldn't be difficult to connect the two.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:11.780
So that's what this is. Are you sure that I can use any date as long as it's

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:15.700
before the end of a person's predetermined lifespan? Well I can't

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:20.140
guarantee it because we Shinigami don't normally work that way but I suppose

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:25.000
anytime before the end of their lifespan should work. I really can't count on you

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:30.000
can I? You got that right? Yes? Yes would you people

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.140
Please hold for a moment.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.250
Ryuzaki, it's Yukita at the NPA.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:38.730
He says he's on the phone with someone from the tip line who has information for us.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:39.210
Right.

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:44.090
Then give Yukita the number for line 5 and ask him to have the informant call that line instead.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:45.430
It'll be safer that way.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.730
Mr. Matsuda, it's okay for you to turn on your cell phone now.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.410
Actually, please turn it on right away.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:52.600
Sure.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:00.000
Yes, this is Suzuki, head of Kira's investigation, public information.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:13.960
Division? Rape Hember's fiancée? Naomi Misora. Heard that name before. So it's her. She's from the

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:20.270
Los Angeles baby murder case. That's right. She was working under me. I guess she must have come

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:30.000
to Japan with her fiancée. Well, apparently she's been missing since the day after her fiancée died.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:34.090
I'm sure that anyone in her situation would be pretty depressed.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:36.980
Was it suicide?

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.980
No, the Naomi Misura I knew was strong,

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:43.060
not to mention she was also an excellent FBI agent.

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:47.710
If anything, it's more likely she'd be trying to catch Kira.

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:49.910
It appears she came to Japan with Penber.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:53.090
It's possible that she may have found a lead.

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:54.190
That's the case.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:57.990
Did Kira manage to get her first?

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.000
Everyone, at this point I'd like to focus our investigation

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.040
on only those people who Ray Pember was tailing.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:06.880
In particular, he was assigned to two police officers

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.920
and those closest to them.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:11.930
Very well, who are these two individuals he was investigating?

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:18.200
Deputy Director Kitamura, along with Detective Superintendent Yagami

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:19.760
and their families.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:23.970
At this stage, I'd like to place wiretaps and surveillance cameras

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:25.730
in both households.

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:30.000
I have to make sure there's no evidence left on this computer, just in case

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:36.330
case someone goes through it. Now I just have to hide these clippings from the

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:42.400
death note in here. It seems like you're pretty skilled with your hands. I bet

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.920
you're pretty popular with the girls aren't you? Skill has nothing to do with

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:51.000
it. It's your looks that count. I'm guessing you're not that popular are you?

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:56.820
Huh? Surveillance cameras? Ryuzaki? I don't see how you could even consider

00:06:56.820 --> 00:07:00.000
this. If this got out we'd have a civil rights scandal on our hands

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.380
We'd all lose our jobs!

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:05.920
You told me you'd be willing to risk your lives for this investigation, but you wouldn't risk your jobs.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:10.530
Ryuzaki, what are the odds that Kiri is in one of those households?

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:15.760
Maybe 10%. No, it's closer to 5%.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.680
Seriously? I'm sorry, but it's not worth the risk.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:24.810
No. Of all the people we've investigated so far, not one of them seemed even the least bit suspicious.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:28.650
Even if there's only a 1% chance, we simply can't afford to ignore it.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:29.410
Chief?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.880
- I don't have to tell you how offended I am

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:34.350
to learn my family is under suspicion.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.370
Having said that, just go ahead with it.

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:39.430
And make sure you install them everywhere.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:41.050
I don't want any blind spots in the house

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:43.460
and that includes the bathroom.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.100
- Thank you very much, that was my intention.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:48.560
- Come on, Chief, you don't have to agree to this.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.520
- Yes, he's right, think about your family.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.780
You have a wife and daughter at home, don't you?

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.970
- Yes, I'm well aware of that fact,

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:56.630
but there is no point in doing any of this

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:57.890
if we can't be thorough.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.600
Now I suggest you keep quiet.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:03.750
I'm sorry.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.990
It's okay.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:07.400
Excuse me.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:15.730
As a courtesy to the Chief and his family, only he and I will conduct surveillance of their home.

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:19.800
Watari, how long will it take to prepare the wiretaps and cameras we need?

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:26.200
Well, starting tomorrow, I can set them up at any time, provided we know when both houses will be empty.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:30.910
See you later, Light.

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:32.650
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:38.540
What? No one's home yet.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:48.310
I'm home!

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:07.810
how's it going i don't think anyone else is in the house right now

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:29.760
do you want to play some video games come on it's been a while you listening light believe it

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:32.060
I never knew he went to such great lengths.

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:35.600
What could he be hiding in there that he doesn't want anyone else to see?

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:39.960
For a 17-year-old kid, I wouldn't say this kind of behavior is particularly abnormal.

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:43.100
When I was his age, I did strange things, too.

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:45.580
Have you ever talked to your son about the investigation?

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:49.800
Of course not. I've never once revealed classified information to my family.

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:53.320
Besides, I don't get to see them too often these days,

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:56.640
and usually as soon as I get home, all I can do is sleep.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:57.840
I understand.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.000
Where exactly?

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:06.430
Where exactly are we going? Light, don't ignore me when I'm talking to you or I'll get

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:14.430
mad. Huh? It doesn't look like these clothes have been bugged. I think we're safe.

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:19.130
Listen to me. There's a very strong possibility that there are wiretaps and maybe surveillance

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:23.840
cameras hidden throughout my house. Really? But that piece of paper was still in your

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:26.830
door, wasn't it? That's true, but...

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:30.000
I left the paper in the door in a way that it would be obvious to anyone entering the

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:35.660
room. The real test is the handle. It is? When that door is closed, the door handle automatically

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:40.500
returns to a horizontal position, and it won't go any higher than that. But whenever I close the

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:44.980
door, I adjust it slightly. Instead of letting it sit horizontally, I lower it by about five

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:49.950
millimeters. When I get home and I try to open the door, if the handle is all the way up, I can be

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:55.150
fairly certain that someone was in my room. That method alone doesn't tell me if my door was

00:10:55.150 --> 00:11:00.000
actually opened. So, I put a mechanical pencil lead in place as well. So,

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.160
What do you do with it?

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:02.510
It goes on the hinge.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:05.170
After I close the door, I take the pencil lead

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:07.110
and rest it on the hinge in such a way that it will

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:09.190
break if the door happens to be opened by anyone.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.150
Normally, I'd take it out myself

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:13.600
when I get back home. When I got home

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.460
from school today, I noticed that the pencil

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:17.410
lead was broken. Now that you

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:19.010
mention it, I do remember that.

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:21.700
First the door handle, then the lead.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.160
I know someone was in there today.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:26.050
Maybe it was your mother. My family

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:27.530
wouldn't have noticed the piece of paper.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.000
What's suspicious is that someone took the

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.830
to put it back in the door.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:34.040
Hi there. Can I help you?

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:35.430
What's this all about?

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:37.910
Are you buying a book about wiretaps and surveillance

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:40.050
so you can figure this mess out?

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:44.080
By the way, Ryuk, what about your apples?

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:45.680
Apples?

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:49.590
That's right, surveillance cameras.

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:52.210
Once the apple's in my mouth, no one can see it.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:54.860
But while I'm holding it, it looks like it's floating.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.140
I thought so.

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:58.620
You told me that Shinigami can't die,

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:00.000
so I guess it won't kill you.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:05.350
stop eating apples for a while don't you think that's a bit much come on i never told you this

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:11.190
but apples are to me what cigarettes and alcohol are to humans do you see what i'm saying i even

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:17.830
get withdrawal symptoms oh yeah what kind of symptoms my body gets all twisted i do handstands

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:24.510
it's not pretty i don't need to see that i know okay here's the thing unfortunately i already gave

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:28.750
I gave Elle the hint that Shinigami love apples, so I just can't afford to take the risk.

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:29.860
When did you...

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:34.210
If it's so important for you to eat apples,

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:37.620
you'll have to find out where all the cameras are hidden.

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:39.860
If you're lucky, you might find a blind spot

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:41.920
where you can eat them without being seen.

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:44.980
All right, let's go.

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:47.920
Yeah, a camera search!

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:50.900
Sounds so interesting.

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:21.450
can't believe my son is looking at those magazines it's normal for a 17 year old but it seems

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:26.820
contrived it's too obvious the only reason he didn't want anyone in his room was because he

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:30.000
had these magazines that's what he wants us to think hey that's my

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:36.250
son you're talking about are you honestly telling me that you suspect him i do suspect him that's

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:40.330
why i placed wiretaps and surveillance cameras in your house in the deputy director's house

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:49.100
i found a camera in the air conditioner so they really put cameras in here they must have bugged

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:53.970
the place as well even if this is the kira case i didn't think the japanese police would ever go

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:59.670
this far this must be l's idea which means they've narrowed down their list of suspects

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.180
By now, they must have figured out that it was someone who Ray Pember was investigating,

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:09.270
or they wouldn't have gone to all this trouble.

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:12.670
Man, these covers mislead you all the time.

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:13.790
No.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:20.000
Given the situation, it's safer if I just assume I'm their prime suspect and the only one being watched.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.550
It'll be okay.

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:26.260
Luckily, I prepared for this kind of situation.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:29.320
Right.

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:33.300
Lie, lie, come on!

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:35.270
Dinner's ready!

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:46.570
I love you.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:49.130
I swear he's perfect!

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:51.020
My class is like that.

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:53.020
Sayu, just eat your dinner.

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:54.490
Wait later!

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:56.580
Hello, Mr. Aizawa.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:58.580
Are the Kitamura's watching television now?

00:14:58.580 --> 00:14:59.640
Yes.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.920
- He's not home, but the other four are watching

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.210
while they eat dinner.

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:05.650
It's channel four.

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:08.020
- Watari, please contact the broadcasters

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:09.540
and tell them to play our message.

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:11.240
- Very well, understood.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.580
- That's right.

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:13.820
- My parents met George Martin.

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:15.420
- What's this?

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:16.640
ICPO?

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.960
They're saying that in response to the Kira murders,

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:20.980
Interpol has decided to dispatch a force

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.260
of 1,500 investigators to Japan.

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:25.780
The investigators were drawn from the law enforcement agencies

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:27.690
of its member nations.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:29.960
1,500 investigators?

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:31.190
Whoa.

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:34.680
Chances are they've got cameras in the living room as well.

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:40.390
Regardless of whether this news is real or not, it's obvious they're just trying to evoke a reaction from me.

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:41.520
Ow.

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:44.210
This is the exact same trick he used last time.

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:47.090
The ICPO sure is stupid.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:48.100
Huh?

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:50.680
I mean, there's no point in making this announcement.

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:54.870
If they're gonna send all these people here to investigate, shouldn't they keep it a secret?

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:59.570
Even the FBI agents who were secretly investigating were killed by Kir.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.430
Why would this be any different?

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:04.930
If you ask me, this is nothing more than a desperate attempt to shock Kira in the hopes

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:06.630
that he'll reveal himself somehow.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:10.880
Quite frankly, I wouldn't be surprised if Kira sees right through this.

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:11.800
Hm.

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:15.140
Your son's clever, isn't he?

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:16.000
Hm.

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:16.930
Well, yes.

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:18.600
Thanks for dinner, Mom.

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:21.330
You're eating a bag of chips?

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:22.750
You just had dinner.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.130
Your good looks are gonna go down the drain if you keep that up.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:27.080
It's a late-night snack for studying.

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.520
- I think that's it, Light.

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:35.180
I found every camera they put in the house.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:38.370
I guess Shinigami get tired when they work hard.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:40.890
Now, let me explain where they all are.

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:43.530
It's a little bit complicated, so listen up.

00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:44.850
There's nothing I hate more

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:46.970
than explaining something twice.

00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:49.810
All right, it's time for me to hit the books.

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:52.410
There sure are a lot of cameras in this room.

00:16:52.410 --> 00:16:54.960
I counted 64 in total.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:56.300
I guess whoever put them here

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:58.880
expected you to at least find some of them.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:00.000
It has to be L.

